Lots of turns, really.

If I am satiated (but I know I'm not almost at the brink) and *really*
need to eat that dragon, I just start eating, and when the game asks if
I want to continue eating, I answer "no". Then I wait twenty turns, and
start eating again. Since I won't get satiated with the first bite, I
eat some more without dying, and get asked the same question.

Again, I wait twenty turns and start eating again. The same question
comes up, and I answer "no" once more. Rinse and repeat: after some
seven or eight tries on average, you'll finish that dragon, without
killing yourself by gluttony.

Since this trick for eating large corpses requires you to start eating
several times over again, I guess that a corpse may stay fresh for over
a hundred and fifty turns or so. Of course, this could also mean that
when you start or continue eating a corpse, the freshness counter is
reset, I'm not sure about that.

By the way, this trick sometimes fails, since once in a while the corpse
will completely rot away and disappear while you're eating it, without
you finishing it and then getting the good effects.

